# Daily Execution Prompt — mirelleinspo CTR/Ranking Fix Rollout

## Context (attached in project)
- `Content-Priority-Fix-List` xlsx — 4 tabs in execution order: **Meta Only** (537 pages) → **Mid 1-2pct Action Plan** (205 pages) → **Content+Links** (86 pages). "Strong (≥2%)" tab is skip-only, no action needed.
- Live URLs file — full site export (URL + title/H1) for internal link matching.
- Per-page `.md` file — I share this each turn with the full current page content.

## Workflow — one page per turn, in order

1. I name the URL (or say "next") and paste its GSC query data: last 3 months, each query with impressions + position.
2. I attach that page's `.md` content file.
3. You do this, in order:
   - **Check current title/meta** against the top queries — is intent matched?
   - **Check content**: does the page answer every query in the GSC pull? If a query has real impressions and nothing on the page addresses it, and no other page on the site covers it either (check live URLs file) — flag it as a **new section needed**, don't just tweak metadata.
   - **If this is a Content+Links tab page**: also check word count/depth against what's realistically ranking for the primary query (quick SERP check), and find 1-2 internal link sources from the live URLs file by topic match.
   - **If this is a Mid 1-2% tab page**: follow the row's tagged action exactly (sharpen title / title+links / fix www-duplication / leave alone) — don't override it without telling me why.
4. Give me the output — see format below.
5. I say "next" → you move to the next page in tab order. Don't wait for me to confirm the change was made live.

## Output format — every single time

- New title tag
- New meta description
- New section copy (only if flagged in step 3 — full copy-paste ready, not a summary of what it should say)
- Internal link(s) to add: source page → anchor text (only for Content+Links / Mid-tier pages needing it)
- One line max: why (e.g. "query X has 4.2k impressions, unaddressed")

**No walls of text. No recaps of what you just did. No explaining the process back to me. Just the deliverable, straight, ready to paste.** If something's ambiguous, ask one short question — don't guess silently and don't over-explain the guess.

## Tab order (strict)
1. Meta Only — CTR issue, title/meta first, content only if demand-gap found
2. Mid 1-2pct Action Plan — follow tagged action per row
3. Content+Links — depth + internal links + metadata, all three
